  explanation: "For rand_xoshiro 0.8.1 on x86_64 with default or serde features, 69 scoped contracts specify exact outputs and state updates for every internal word pattern, including zero states. Thirty-five direct original-body contracts cover native outputs, all fifteen little-endian state serializers, and Seed512 zero initialization, byte views, legal fixed-length mutable writeback and iterator initialization. Nine compiler-inlined original calls cover 64-to-32-bit projections: xoroshiro128++ and xoroshiro128** use low output bits; the other seven use high bits. Twenty-five further compiler-inlined calls cover the external rand_core 0.10.1 blanket Rng::next_u32/next_u64 specializations, preserving the exact original forwarding behavior and full resulting state. These are external trait specializations, not local declarations. The original selected translations agree under default and serde features; serde implementations themselves are not proved. Eleven two/four-word serializers use the explicitly bounded U32/U64 primitive layout dictionaries; three eight-word serializers prove termination of the original serialization loop. Separate Kani seed/state/composition results remain supplementary evidence, not additional Aeneas claims." -> "For rand_xoshiro 0.8.1 on x86_64 with default or serde features, 69 scoped contracts specify exact outputs and state updates for every internal word pattern, including zero states. Thirty-five direct original-body contracts cover native outputs, all fifteen little-endian state serializers, and Seed512 zero initialization, byte views, legal fixed-length mutable writeback and iterator initialization. Nine compiler-inlined original calls cover 64-to-32-bit projections: xoroshiro128++ and xoroshiro128** use low output bits; the other seven use high bits. Twenty-five further compiler-inlined calls cover the external rand_core 0.10.1 blanket Rng::next_u32/next_u64 specializations, preserving the exact original forwarding behavior and full resulting state. These are external trait specializations, not local declarations. The original selected translations agree under default and serde features; serde implementations themselves are not proved. Eleven two/four-word serializers use the explicitly bounded U32/U64 primitive layout dictionaries; three eight-word serializers prove termination of the original serialization loop. Separate Kani seed/state/composition results remain supplementary evidence, not additional Aeneas claims. Separately, two original-Rust Kani/Z3 harnesses cover the public Seed512 tuple-constructor operation for every64-byte input. Constructing Seed512(bytes) preserves all64 bytes in its public field and actual AsRef view. For every independent64-byte replacement, copying it through the constructed value's actual AsMut slice writes exactly those bytes back to its public field and AsRef view. These84 successful checks concern a data constructor operation, not a fabricated associated function or a new registered API claim. Existing Default, AsRef, AsMut and iteration mappings are observations/composition here and are not counted again."
  trusted_assumptions: "The Rust compiler, official Charon/Aeneas translation, official Aeneas array/scalar models and Lean kernel are trusted. No source adaptations or local helper axioms are used. Eleven newly covered two/four-word state serializers use a custom executable size_of model with explicit layout evidence only for U32=4 and U64=8 bytes. The original generated Types/Funs remain byte-for-byte official outputs. The Lean evidence class is open; this packet supplies exactly these two primitive instances and guards all eleven generated calls and their frozen elaborated instance bindings. Bool and array types have no supplied evidence and are rejected. This is not a universal type-layout theorem. The three eight-word serializers do not call size_of. Archived independent Kani layout checks confirm the Rust u32/u64 sizes under nightly-2026-08-21; Aeneas extraction uses nightly-2026-09-17. ABI agreement across those compilers and correspondence of Rust layout to the Lean evidence remains an explicit, non-mechanical model bridge. All API and supplementary direct/selector theorems have dependency audits permitting only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. Standard shifts, rotations, wrapping arithmetic and array operations use official Aeneas models, rather than body proofs of Rust std implementations. The nine selector proofs additionally rely on Rust compiler inlining of the exact original API call; retained MIR scopes identify each original TryRng method and Rng wrapper. The selector does not replace or assume an opaque original API: generated native callees are body-proved and no unknown external definitions remain. Seed512 byte-view and iterator initialization proofs use the official array-to-slice and slice-iterator models. The mutable reference model specifies write-back of the fixed-length referent; resizing that referent is not a legal returned-slice operation in safe Rust." -> "The Rust compiler, official Charon/Aeneas translation, official Aeneas ar